WEBVTT

00:34:29.830 --> 00:34:32.296
worrying isn't necessarily a bad thing.

00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:35.676
SK: One of the things
that NASA does very well is,

00:34:35.700 --> 00:34:38.056
and how we operate in space is,

00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:40.487
we're always having to think about,

00:34:40.511 --> 00:34:42.273
"OK, what is the next worst thing

00:34:42.297 --> 00:34:44.714
that can happen to us right now?

00:34:44.738 --> 00:34:48.606
And how do we react and respond to that?"

00:34:48.630 --> 00:34:53.466
You know, in some ways
that can cause stress and anxiety.

00:34:53.490 --> 00:34:56.239
AG: There's a distinction
that we often make in psychology

00:34:56.263 --> 00:34:57.835
between worrying and rumination,

00:34:57.859 --> 00:35:00.804
where worrying is basically
an attempt at problem-solving